      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pack cementation at approximately 900°C for 2 hours in an inert atmosphere will introduce an Al-enriched surface on HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-enriched surface will form Al2O3 during subsequent exposure to air at 1100–1200°C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 scale will be continuous.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 scale will be adherent to the refractory HEA.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 scale will grow slowly under the specified high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al2O3 has very low diffusivity for oxygen and metal ions.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low oxygen and metal-ion diffusivity through the Al2O3 scale will retard further oxidation of the substrate.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aluminized HfNbTaTiZr will have significantly better oxygen resistance than untreated HfNbTaTiZr during exposure to air at 1100–1200°C for up to 100 hours.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Aluminized samples will exhibit significantly lower oxidation-induced mass gain than untreated samples.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
